10
00:44:20,869 --> 00:44:26,869
The Crow is a 1994 American gothic supernatural superhero film
directed by Alex Proyas and written by David J.

11
00:48:46,956 --> 00:48:52,956
Schow and John Shirley, based on the 1989 comic book series by James O'Barr.

12
00:53:13,043 --> 00:53:19,043
It stars Brandon Lee in his final film role, as Eric Draven, a rock musician who is resurrected
from the dead to seek vengeance against the gang who murdered him and his fiancée.

13
00:57:39,130 --> 00:57:45,130
Lee was fatally wounded by a prop gun during filming.

14
01:02:05,217 --> 01:02:11,217
As he had finished most of his scenes, the film was completed through
script rewrites, a stunt double and digital effects.

15
01:06:31,304 --> 01:06:37,304
After Lee's death, Paramount Pictures opted out of distribution
and the rights were acquired by Miramax Films.

16
01:10:57,391 --> 01:11:03,391
The film is dedicated to Lee and his fiancée, Eliza Hutton.

17
01:15:23,478 --> 01:15:29,478
The Crow premiered in Santa Monica on May 10, 1994, and was released in
the United States on May 13, 1994, by Dimension Films.

18
01:19:49,565 --> 01:19:55,565
The film received positive reviews for its stylized noir
aesthetic, emotional resonance and Lee's performance.

19
01:24:15,652 --> 01:24:21,652
It grossed $94 million on a $23 million budget and has gained a cult following.

20
01:28:41,739 --> 01:28:47,739
The success led to three sequels, a television series, and a 2024 reboot,
all of which failed to replicate the first movie's success.

21
01:33:07,826 --> 01:33:13,826
The film explores themes of martial arts,
superhero, supernatural, halloween, crow.

22
01:37:33,913 --> 01:37:39,913
The tone is dark and intense.
